---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Terms of use" description="The terms of use for the Access:Hull website.">

  <section class="ah-sec" aria-labelledby="tm-h"><div class="ah-in lg-wrap">
    <nav class="lg-nav" aria-label="Policies"><a href="/accessibility/">Accessibility statement</a><a href="/privacy/">Privacy notice</a><a href="/cookies/">Cookies</a><a href="/terms/" aria-current="page">Terms of use</a></nav>
    <article class="lg">
      <p class="ah-eyebrow">Policies</p>
      <h1 id="tm-h">Terms of use</h1>
      <p class="lg-up">Last updated 2 October 2026</p>
      <p class="lg-lead">These terms apply to your use of the Access:Hull website. By using the site you agree to them.</p>

      <h2>About us</h2>
      <p>This website is run by <span class="ph">[legal name of the organisation]</span> for the Access:Hull Digital Inclusion Programme. Registered address: <span class="ph">[registered address]</span>.</p>

      <h2>Information on this website</h2>
      <p>We work hard to keep the information here accurate and up to date, but we can't guarantee it. In particular:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Prices and offers:</b> social tariffs, free SIM allowances and eligibility rules are set by the providers and can change. Always check with the provider before signing up.</li>
        <li><b>Hubs and services:</b> opening times and what's on offer may change. Please call ahead.</li>
        <li><b>Data and maps:</b> ward figures come from published sources such as the English Indices of Deprivation 2025, the Census 2021 and Ofcom. They describe areas, not individual households, and may contain errors or be revised by the original publishers.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Nothing on this site is financial, legal or professional advice.</p>

      <h2>Using our content</h2>
      <p>The Access:Hull name and logo belong to us and may only be used with our permission. Partners can request the logo by <a href="/contact/">contacting us</a>.</p>
      <p>Statistics drawn from public sources are available under the Open Government Licence. You're welcome to quote them, crediting the original source.</p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You must not use this website to break the law, send spam, upload harmful code, or try to get unauthorised access to the site or its data. Please don't submit false information through our forms.</p>

      <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
      <p>We link to other websites to help you find support. We're not responsible for their content or how they handle your information.</p>

      <h2>Our liability</h2>
      <p>We are not liable for any loss caused by relying on information on this site, or by the site being unavailable, as far as the law allows. Nothing in these terms limits liability that can't legally be limited.</p>

      <h2>Changes and governing law</h2>
      <p>We may update these terms from time to time. The date at the top shows when they last changed. These terms are governed by the law of England and Wales.</p>
    </article>
  </div></section>

</Base>
